# A generic x86-64 PC that boots by UEFI: what every such PC needs. Its kernel is not
# in the base (kernel-lts). Its configuration files are in rootfs/.
# the EFI system partition: a FAT file system, checked and written by these
dosfstools
# the firmware's boot entries
efibootmgr
# kernel updates on the boot partition (HANDOFF=uefi), the verdict at boot, and the
# rollback after the loader's limit (GlassineOS/boot)
glassine-bootimg
# a kernel set's boot modules archive, made on the PC by GlassineOS/boot's
# build-boot-modules.sh (the uefi hand-off): modprobe/depmod and the archive
cpio
kmod
